Package: rocket-compiler
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Multi-Arch: foreign
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.iree-rocket.nocompiler>
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests:
 iree-rocket-tools,
Description: IREE model compiler with the Rockchip RK3588 NPU (Rocket) target
 rocket-compiler compiles ONNX-imported MLIR models into IREE .vmfb modules
 that run convolutions, matmuls, pooling and elementwise work on the RK3588
 NPU through the mainline "rocket" accel driver, and everything else on the
 CPU. It also explains, per operation, why each candidate did or did not
 offload (the "audit" subcommand).
 .
 The package carries its own build of IREE's libIREECompiler.so with the
 Rocket target plugin compiled in, plus the iree-lld linker it needs, in a
 private directory. Neither is meant to be used by anything else, and
 neither conflicts with an upstream IREE installation.
 .
 Compiling does not need the NPU, so the package is useful on a desktop
 that cross-compiles models for the board. Modules run on the IREE runtime
 of the same version: iree-rocket-tools, or libiree-rocket-runtime314.

# The package name carries the SONAME, which follows IREE's version
# (rocket-runtime/CMakeLists.txt): libiree_rocket_runtime.so.314 for IREE
# 3.14. An IREE bump renames this package; debian/rules fails the build if the
# two disagree.
Package: libiree-rocket-runtime314
Section: libs
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.iree-rocket.noruntime>
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: IREE runtime with the Rockchip RK3588 NPU (Rocket) HAL driver
 libiree_rocket_runtime is IREE's runtime, the Rocket HAL driver for the
 RK3588 NPU (mainline "rocket" accel driver, /dev/accel/accel0) and a small
 session API (rocket/runtime.h) in one shared library. It runs the .vmfb
 modules rocket-compiler produces, on the NPU and the CPU together.
 .
 Opening the NPU needs read and write access to /dev/accel/accel0, which
 Debian's udev rules give the "render" group.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

Package: libiree-rocket-runtime-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.iree-rocket.noruntime>
Depends:
 libiree-rocket-runtime314 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: IREE runtime with the RK3588 NPU (Rocket) HAL driver - development files
 libiree_rocket_runtime is IREE's runtime, the Rocket HAL driver for the
 RK3588 NPU and a small session API (rocket/runtime.h) in one shared library.
 .
 This package contains the headers (rocket/runtime.h and IREE's runtime
 headers, under /usr/include/iree-rocket-runtime), pkg-config files
 (iree-rocket-runtime, iree-rocket-runtime-static), a CMake package
 (find_package(IreeRocketRuntime)), the static archive and two samples.
 The rocket-runtime Rust crate finds the library through pkg-config.

Package: iree-rocket-tools
Architecture: arm64
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.iree-rocket.noruntime>
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests:
 rocket-compiler,
Description: run IREE modules on the Rockchip RK3588 NPU (Rocket)
 Command-line tools for the .vmfb modules rocket-compiler produces:
 .
  * rocket-run-module: runs one function through the libiree-rocket-runtime
    session API, with the NPU and CPU devices set up the way rocket-compiler
    expects;
  * iree-rocket-run-module and iree-rocket-benchmark-module: IREE's
    iree-run-module and iree-benchmark-module with the Rocket HAL driver
    linked in, renamed so they never collide with an upstream IREE install.
